// The authored source of elder_wei_intro.tres (ADR 0862).
// Compile with:
//   uv run python -m tools dialogue compile \
//     --src game/data/dialogue/elder_wei_intro.yarn \
//     --npc elder_wei --id elder_wei_intro \
//     --out res://data/dialogue/elder_wei_intro.tres
//
// `-> #id label` names a choice's id so a saved press is addressed by name rather than
// by position (DialogueChoiceDef's own rule).
title: intro
---
elder_wei: You climb like someone who has read the register.
elder_wei: Ask me what you came to ask.
-> #ask_oath Ask whose oath is written in that book. <<set $asked_about_the_oath = true>> <<jump oath>>
===
title: oath
---
elder_wei: An oath is a debt a body agrees to carry.
elder_wei: Mine is older than this mountain and I am still paying it.
-> #ask_debt Then ask who holds the debt now. <<if $regard >= 2>> <<jump debt>>
-> #leave Say nothing more.
===
title: debt
---
elder_wei: Whoever is still standing when the book closes.
elder_wei: That is the whole of it, and it is not a small thing to say.
-> #leave Say nothing more.
===
